# MLOps Architecture Rules

## Three-Layer Separation

### Layer 1 — Training Pipeline (`src/training/`)
- Data ingestion + validation (Pandera schema check)
- Feature engineering (pure functions, no side effects)
- Model training (fit + evaluate)
- MLflow logging (params, metrics, artifacts)
- Model registration (only if gates pass)

### Layer 2 — Model Registry (MLflow)
- Models are registered with `name`, `version`, `stage` (Staging → Production)
- Every version has a description artifact: training data source, eval metrics, limitations
- Staging = passed eval gate, not yet A/B tested
- Production = passed A/B test or manual promotion by ML engineer

### Layer 3 — Serving Layer (`src/serving/`)
- FastAPI app with single `/predict` endpoint
- Loads model at startup: `mlflow.pyfunc.load_model(f"models:/{MODEL_NAME}/Production")`
- No business logic in serving — only schema validation + model.predict() + response formatting
- Health check endpoint: `/health` returns model name + version currently loaded

## Directory Structure
```
src/
  training/
    pipeline.py        # orchestrates the full training run
    features.py        # pure feature engineering functions
    evaluate.py        # evaluation metrics + threshold checks
    validate.py        # Pandera schema + distribution checks
  serving/
    main.py            # FastAPI app
    schemas.py         # Pydantic request/response models
    loader.py          # mlflow.pyfunc.load_model() wrapper
  shared/
    config.py          # pydantic-settings config (env vars)
    logging.py         # structured logging setup
tests/
  unit/
    test_features.py   # pure function tests (no MLflow)
    test_validate.py   # schema validation tests
  integration/
    test_pipeline.py   # full pipeline with tmp MLflow tracking URI
    test_serving.py    # FastAPI test client
data/
  fixtures/
    train_sample.csv   # small fixed fixture for CI
    validation.csv     # held-out fixture for eval tests
mlruns/               # local MLflow tracking (gitignored)
```

## MLflow Tracking Structure
- Experiment name: `{project}/{component}` (e.g., `churn/v2-xgboost`)
- Run tags: `git_commit`, `data_hash`, `triggered_by` (manual/ci/scheduled)
- Logged artifacts: trained model, feature importance plot, confusion matrix, requirements.txt
